      "message": "The point is that we had a proliferation of slightly different IP string conversions functions.  Frank made the point in https://review.gerrithub.io/c/ffilz/nfs-ganesha/+/1209432 and I think I also noted it at the time.  \n\nThe code is moving to IPv6.  This function works as a partner to  cmp_sockaddr().  It is already used twice in nfs4_recovery.c\n\nYou have ip_str_to_int  in recovery_ados_cluster.c - which is where I stole the basics from.  \n\nThere is now  hash_sockaddr() in rpc_tools used as well in recovery_ados_cluster.c .  The ipV4 bytes are in the reverse order there and the IPv6 bytes are different.  I see that the byte order in ip_str_to_int() is intuitive to read in the purpose it is used. \n\nI have some other work I was doing and will submit soon,  I had a copy of your ip_str_to_int(), so I thought that was a candidate for moving somewhere common.  I probably won\u0027t be using that now, when I revisit the code.",
